d4bd125bc","position":"1793300885962081854-59e27bd0-a344-4957-af8c-c42be43fc1fd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0ac9653ad6b146e107e0818ddb0f7445dfcdf3e052a48352874a8b9f7243322e","event_uuid":"6a266f58-3d46-4e47-a66a-c793297123cf","position":{"commit_sha":"0a29c3c3dfea537cf701f59ec50efc105a6cfee4","position":"1793312148086289534-6a266f58-3d46-4e47-a66a-c793297123cf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793300272444087806,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"da0a0e2d-8d96-4b68-b39d-7fa22ad7abe1","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"a256-1ae4-cf3d-4711"},{"link_uuid":"6a266f58-3d46-4e47-a66a-c793297123cf","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a772-ab5e-871f-406b"}],"description":"# Repoint the remaining reviewer-stand-in tests off `ticket-quality`\n\n## Context\n\nEpic 87d8 is retiring the `ticket-quality` reviewer prompt. The prompt cannot be\ndeleted while tests still name it, so its users are repointed slice by slice first.\nThe previous slice took the two largest files (31 references). This slice takes every\nremaining *stand-in* use: a test that needs some packaged reviewer id and happens to\nhave picked this one.\n\nSeven files hold 25 such references. None of them is testing `ticket-quality` itself:\n\n- `tests/unit/test_prompt_library_writes.py` (8) — `enumerate_library` coverage. Its\n  own comment reads \"a packaged reviewer\", and one assertion checks that a reviewer\n  is absent from `enumerate_criteria`.\n- `tests/unit/test_prompt_index.py` (7) — `get_prompt` resolution and user-override\n  precedence, including an override whose front-matter declares a `dimension`.\n- `tests/unit/test_prompts_git_canonical.py` (4) — canonical render metadata and\n  missing-variable raising.\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py` (3) — catalog membership and\n  `llm.get_prompt` render metadata.\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_agent_op_safeguard.py` (1) — a workflow-document\n  fixture naming any prompt in a step.\n- `tests/unit/test_generated_surface_markers.py` (1) — catalog membership.\n- `tests/external/test_pydantic_ai_cutover_live.py` (1) — a workflow-step fixture.\n\n## Approach\n\nSubstitute the id `ticket-quality` with `code-quality` and the stem `ticket_quality`\nwith `code_quality` throughout those seven files. No test is added, deleted, renamed,\nor restructured, and no assertion changes meaning.\n\n`code-quality` matches `ticket-quality` on every property these tests depend on,\nverified by reading both prompts' front-matter rather than assumed:\n\n- `category: review`, so it is in the reviewer catalog and `get_prompt` resolves it.\n- `inputs: reviewer_input` and `outputs: review_result` — identical contract.\n- `execution_mode: agentic` — identical.\n- The same two template variables, `{{ticket_id}}` and `{{ticket_context}}`, which is\n  what `test_prompts_git_canonical.py`'s missing-variable test depends on.\n- **No `applies_to` globs.** `security` and `tests` declare them, so either would\n  change `select_reviewers` results. `code-quality` declares none, as\n  `ticket-quality` does.\n\n`completion-verifier` was rejected: its `outputs` is `completion_verdict`.\n`spec-alignment` matches on contract but is the batch spec-scan reviewer.\n\nTwo further references are deliberately NOT in this slice, because they are roster\nenumerations rather than stand-ins and can only shrink when the prompt is actually\ndeleted: `tests/unit/test_prompt_front_matter.py:183` (the minimum packaged-id set\nthat keeps the golden round-trip from passing on nothing) and\n`tests/unit/test_prompt_cache_split.py:32` (`_MARKED_PROMPTS`, a parametrize tuple —\nremoving an entry changes node IDs). Both belong with the prompt's deletion.\n\n## Scope\n\nVerified rather than assumed: the substitution was applied to a clean checkout of\n`3b80ff04452` and the six locally-runnable files' 110 tests were run. All 110 passed\nwith no other edit, and the collected node IDs were byte-identical to the baseline.\n`git grep -cF` over the seven files then returned nothing. `ruff check` passed with\nno reformatting required.\n\n`tests/external/test_pydantic_ai_cutover_live.py` carries the `external` marker, so\nit is excluded from `make test` and from CI's gating cell. Its single-line change is\ncovered by the grep and lint criteria below, not by a test run.\n\nOut of scope, and deliberately untouched: the prompt file\n`src/rebar/llm/reviewers/ticket_quality.md`, `reviewers/index.json`, the two roster\nenumerations named above, `docs/` prose, and the workflow example YAML. The prompt\nstays in the catalog after this slice; later slices retire it.\n\nAlso out of scope, because each is a frozen or derived artifact rather than a live\nreference: `docs/release-notes.md` historical entries, the\n`evals/plan-review-gate/runs/*.jsonl` input corpora, and the tracked `.test_durations`\npytest-split timing cache.\n\n`docs/release-notes.md` gains one short entry recording the fixture repoint, with no\nchange to test count, test names, or behaviour. The entry is additions-only.\n\n## Testing\n\nNo new tests. These files are themselves the tests, and they must keep passing\nunchanged in count and in name. Their collected node IDs are compared before and\nafter to prove the slice neither adds nor removes a test.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nEvery command below was run against `3b80ff04452` while writing this plan.\n`$F8` below names the seven files listed in Context.\n\n- [ ] **AC1** `git grep -cF -e 'ticket-quality' -e 'ticket_quality' -- $F8` prints\n      nothing and exits 1. Today it prints 8, 7, 4, 3, 1, 1 and 1.\n- [ ] **AC2** `pytest $F8 -q` (external file omitted, as it cannot run locally) exits\n      0 reporting exactly `110 passed`.\n- [ ] **AC3** `pytest $F8 -q --collect-only | grep '::' | sort` (external file\n      omitted) is byte-identical to the same command on `origin/main`. No test name\n      contains a reviewer id, so the lists must match exactly.\n- [ ] **AC4** `git diff --numstat origin/main...HEAD` lists exactly those seven files\n      plus `docs/release-notes.md`, and no other path.\n- [ ] **AC5** `ruff check src tests` exits 0 with no output.\n- [ ] **AC6** `git diff --numstat origin/main...HEAD -- docs/release-notes.md` shows a\n      non-zero addition count and `0` deletions.\n- [ ] **AC7** `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_prompt_library_writes.py","reason":"repoint 8 enumerate_library stand-in references to code-quality"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_prompt_index.py","reason":"repoint 7 get_prompt/override-precedence stand-in references to code-quality"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_prompts_git_canonical.py","reason":"repoint 4 canonical-render stand-in references to code-quality"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py","reason":"repoint 3 catalog-membership and render-metadata references to code-quality"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_agent_op_safeguard.py","reason":"repoint the workflow-document fixture prompt id to code-quality"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_generated_surface_markers.py","reason":"repoint the catalog-membership assertion to code-quality"},{"path":"tests/external/test_pydantic_ai_cutover_live.py","reason":"repoint the workflow-step fixture prompt id to code-quality"},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"record the fixture repoint; additions only"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","87d8-8bb6-5226-4a5b"],["relates_to","a772-ab5e-871f-406b"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"87d8-8bb6-5226-4a5b","parent_status_uuid":"d9107aa0-a25f-4b6e-ad88-f3295404bc5d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d4ca-0470-d792-49df","ticket_type":"story","title":"Repoint reviewer-stand-in tests off ticket-quality","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["35b8bc06-a9b7-44c1-801c-aac62c4e627a","7e4b8b20-b820-42ab-ab6a-83d960364a4f","da0a0e2d-8d96-4b68-b39d-7fa22ad7abe1","f1e2cb04-4f10-41ed-ba25-7767a7851474","d9107aa0-a25f-4b6e-ad88-f3295404bc5d","59e27bd0-a344-4957-af8c-c42be43fc1fd","6a266f58-3d46-4e47-a66a-c793297123cf"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793312148086289535,"uuid":"b5b16056-fcea-43f3-99ff-5059ab6fba5b"}